1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,480
Listen to this sound.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:03,400
Ch!

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,080
Two spellings can make it.

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:11,210
We can write ch, or we can write tch.

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:13,770
Say it with me.

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:15,060
Ch!

7
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:20,800
You hear it in chair, and you hear it in catch.

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,400
It is the same sound, but the spelling is different.

9
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:29,940
So how do we know which one to write?

10
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:35,680
This time we look at the letter just before the sound.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,200
Here is the rule.

12
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:44,900
If the sound comes right after a short vowel, we write tch.

13
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:46,960
Listen.

14
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,840
C - a - tch.

15
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:52,900
Catch!

16
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:59,060
That a is a short vowel, so this word takes tch.

17
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,640
Here are more.

18
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:03,740
Match.

19
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:05,860
Watch.

20
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,360
Fetch.

21
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:13,760
They all have a short vowel first, and then tch.

22
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:19,740
In every other place, we simply write ch.

23
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,030
There are three of those places.

24
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,910
The first is at the start of a word.

25
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:29,780
Chair.

26
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,000
Chin.

27
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:33,780
Chip.

28
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:39,120
Nothing comes before the sound, so we write ch.

29
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:44,080
The second is after a consonant.

30
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:49,520
A consonant is any letter that is not a vowel.

31
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,940
Listen to lunch, and bench.

32
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,540
There is an n before the sound, so we write ch.

33
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:06,770
The third is after a long vowel.

34
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:11,100
A long vowel says its own name.

35
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:19,380
Listen to beach, coach and peach.

36
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:25,200
Those vowels are long, so we write ch again.

37
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,680
But watch out!

38
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,480
Some words break this rule.

39
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:35,320
Let's call them the rule breakers.

40
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:40,780
There are nine you will meet a lot, so let's learn them.

41
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,980
First come four little words.

42
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:46,720
Much.

43
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:48,620
Such.

44
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:50,860
Rich.

45
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:52,940
Which.

46
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,300
All four have short vowels, so they should take tch.

47
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,250
But they don't!

48
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,460
They just use ch.

49
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:06,630
So why are they different?

50
00:03:08,220 --> 00:03:09,380
Here is the funny part.

51
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:12,900
These four are older than the rule!

52
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,980
People were writing them a very long time ago.

53
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:22,560
The rule came along later, but these four were already here.

54
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,300
So they never had to change.

55
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,800
Here is a trick to help you remember them.

56
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,820
They go together in two pairs that rhyme.

57
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,540
Much and such.

58
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:39,020
Rich and which.

59
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:43,790
Say them in pairs, and they will stay in your head.

60
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:48,980
Then come five longer rule breakers.

61
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:51,260
Sandwich.

62
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,300
Spinach.

63
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:55,540
Ostrich.

64
00:03:58,660 --> 00:03:58,880
Attach.

65
00:03:58,880 --> 00:03:59,240
Detach.

66
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:05,330
They have short vowels too, but they still use ch.

67
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:10,280
These five travelled here from lands far away.

68
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:14,800
They packed their own spelling and brought it with them.

69
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:19,340
And when they arrived, they simply kept it!

70
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,980
So we learn these five by remembering them.

71
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,020
Now let's say all nine together.

72
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:37,840
Much, such, rich, which.

73
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:48,760
Sandwich, spinach, ostrich, attach, detach.

74
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,500
Remember those nine, and the rule will work for the rest!

75
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,880
Now let's look at more tch words.

76
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:00,980
Catch.

77
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:02,980
Match.

78
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,120
Watch.

79
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:07,200
Fetch.

80
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:09,720
Itch.

81
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,060
Ditch.

82
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:18,070
Every one of them has a short vowel, and then tch.

83
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,860
And now let's look at the ch words.

84
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,060
Chair.

85
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:25,920
Chin.

86
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,240
Chip.

87
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:30,640
Lunch.

88
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:32,980
Beach.

89
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:35,180
Coach.

90
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:47,360
At the start, after a consonant, or after a long vowel, we write just ch.

91
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,170
Now it is your turn!

92
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:52,460
Here is the word.

93
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:53,480
Beach.

94
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:59,020
Do we write it with ch, or with tch?

95
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,340
It is ch!

96
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:07,480
Here, e and a make a long vowel, not a short one.

97
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,440
So let's remember it together.

98
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:15,210
After a short vowel we write tch.

99
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:20,240
Everywhere else we write just ch.

100
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,520
And don't forget our nine rule breakers.

101
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:29,940
Come and practise these words in the English Learning app.

102
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:33,080
It is free, with no ads!
